OL,3,GNEWSAHow a teacake tycoon helped to
OL,4,Asave a village's lifeboat station
OL,5,
OL,6,FA decade ago there was a day of
OL,7,Fcelebration in the little Borders
OL,8,Fcoastal village of St Abbs that they
OL,9,Fwill never forget.
OL,11,FThe RNLI closed its lifeboat station in
OL,12,F2015 - bringing a 104-year association
OL,13,Fto an end - saying there was no clear
OL,14,Fneed for it with one nearby in
OL,15,FEyemouth.
OL,17,FThe community rallied round to raise
OL,18,Fthe money needed to bring a boat back
OL,19,Fand found a surprise ally in the shape
OL,20,Fof the teacake tycoon Sir Boyd Tunnock.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,427,420,260,160,0,100
